# Proxy pool for the multi-account build.
#
# One proxy per line. Each enabled account is bound to its own entry, and the
# binding is written into accounts.json, so the exit IP of an account stays the
# same across restarts - a stable exit is worth more than a rotating one when it
# comes to automated account checks.
#
# Copy this file to `proxies.txt` next to the program and fill in your ports.
#
# With Clash / mihomo, a port alone does not give you a different exit: every
# connection through any mixed-port still leaves through whatever the rules
# pick, so N ports share one IP. What pins an exit is the `proxy` field of a
# listener - that inbound uses it directly and skips the rules. Add one
# listener per account, with a FIXED-IP node (not url-test/load-balance, those
# drift), on ports clear of the ones Clash Verge manages (7897/7898/7899):
#
#   listeners:
#     - {name: acct-1, type: mixed, port: 7901, proxy: US-Fixed-01, udp: true}
#     - {name: acct-2, type: mixed, port: 7902, proxy: TW-Fixed-01, udp: true}
#
# In Clash Verge, put that in the Merge template of the active profile. Editing
# config.yaml directly does nothing useful - it is regenerated.
#
# Lines starting with # are ignored. Blank lines are ignored.
# A line without a scheme is treated as http://host:port.

127.0.0.1:7901
127.0.0.1:7902
127.0.0.1:7903
127.0.0.1:7904
127.0.0.1:7905
